            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Can't `opts` be removed from the documentation here. Isn't it just a normal optional parameter of type `dict` now?\n\n> Explicitly passing a nil value is an error.\n\nIf I have a function with 2 or more optional parameters, how do I pass only the 2nd one. Is it by passing an empty dict as the first parameter even if it is an integer (or something else that isn't a dict)? Wouldn't `nil` be more natural as it can be any type?",
            "commit_id": "ef34c598917c82462b147563e15d52be2fba3899",
            "created_at": "2026-07-13T18:39:00Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -244,6 +245,9 @@ As Nvim evolves the API may change in compliance with this CONTRACT:\n     new return value.\n   - An optional `opts` parameter may be ADDED.\n   - Optional parameters may be ADDED following an `opts` parameter.\n+  - The `opts` parameter and any following parameters MAY BE OMITTED by the\n+    client (equivalent to passing an empty dict). Explicitly passing a nil\n+    value is an error.",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40720#discussion_r3573235229",
