            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Can't `opts` be removed from the documentation here. Isn't it just a normal optional parameter of type `dict`\r\n\r\nIn our C API layer we currently have no way to express \"optional\", so the `opts` parameter name is the way to do that. If anyone wants to introduce something fancy like a `API_OPTIONAL()` macro, I'm happy to merge it.\r\n\r\nHowever, you're right that there is no need to mention this in the api-contract, since the metadata returns the `optional` flag. I will update the docs\r\n\r\n\r\n> how do I pass only the 2nd one. Is it by passing an empty dict as the first parameter even if it is an integer\r\n\r\nCurrently only Dict/Array can be optional. We can of course improve this. There are no such cases at all right now, so it's not an urgent problem...",
            "commit_id": "ef34c598917c82462b147563e15d52be2fba3899",
            "created_at": "2026-07-13T18:46:12Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -244,6 +245,9 @@ As Nvim evolves the API may change in compliance with this CONTRACT:\n     new return value.\n   - An optional `opts` parameter may be ADDED.\n   - Optional parameters may be ADDED following an `opts` parameter.\n+  - The `opts` parameter and any following parameters MAY BE OMITTED by the\n+    client (equivalent to passing an empty dict). Explicitly passing a nil\n+    value is an error.",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40720#discussion_r3573278319",
            "id": 3573278319,
            "in_reply_to_id": 3573235229,
            "line": 250,
            "node_id": "PRRC_kwDOAPphoM7U--Zv",
            "original_commit_id": "ef34c598917c82462b147563e15d52be2fba3899",
            "original_line": 250,
